<title>GERMANY: Gerresheimer buys stake in Belgian glass maker.</title>
<headline>Gerresheimer buys stake in Belgian glass maker.</headline>
<dateline>DUESSELDORF, Germany 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's Gerresheimer Glas AG said on Thursday that it has bought a majority stake in Belgian glass producer Nouvelles Verreries de Momignies.</p>
<p>Gerresheimer said it bought the 60 percent stake in the group, which is based in Momignies, from the German-based Heinz Gruppe.</p>
<p>No details of the sale price were given.</p>
<p>Nouvelles Verreries, which employs about 700 workers, is a manufacturer of perfume, cosmetic and pharmaceutical packaging and has annual sales of about 100 million marks.</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
